+## Step-18b (task approval): written 2026-11-02; first CI run red on node-db, fixed by `step-18b-fix.patch` (CI of the fix not yet seen)
+
+- **First run, `910522334a333e561701b50ed2dbbc92f459d5ba`:** node-api 1011 in 256 suites and web 928 in 98 files green; node-db 375 of 378 (3 failed). Causes: (1) `Stages.RequiresApproval` has a Node-only `DEFAULT false` and `efSchema.integration.test.js` allows only the ten array defaults (two failed subtests); (2) **a real bug, not new in 18b's logic:** the worker start, pause and resume update in `orderRoutes.js` used `$1` twice (`"Status" = $1` and `CASE WHEN $1 = ...`), so PostgreSQL answered 42P08 and the three routes returned 500 on a real database; no earlier test had run them against PostgreSQL (the approval suite's reject-then-resume subtest found it).
+- **Fix:** the `CASE` now reads its own parameter (`$5::text`); `Stages.RequiresApproval` joins the Node-only defaults list in `test/db/helpers.js` (so the "no defaults" test and the no-defaults registration test cover it); register-business now writes `"RequiresApproval"` (FALSE) when it creates the default stages; new restricted-role subtest in `taskApproval.integration.test.js` runs start, a refused second start, pause and resume and checks the task events. No migration, no route change.
 
 - Migration `0046_task_approval.sql`: `Stages.RequiresApproval` (default false) and `ProductionTasks.ApprovalNote`, `ApprovalDecidedByUserId`, `ApprovalDecidedAtUtc`. Migrations now end at `0046`; next free number `0047`.
 - Flow: a worker completes a task of an approval stage and it becomes `AwaitingApproval` (no completion time). Dependents and the order keep waiting because they already wait for `Completed`. A manager (`tasks.manage`, location-scoped) approves (`Completed`, dependents released) or rejects with a note (`Paused`, note shown to the worker, who resumes and resubmits; a new submission clears the note). The assignee cannot decide their own task.
